title: 'v7.2 T-005: enforcement verifies completion, not invocation (Teeth complete)'
summary: 'Shipped the unshipped third leg of v7''s ''Teeth.'' The .orchestrated enforcement marker was written on orchestrate_inline tool ENTRY for every mode — so a single mode=quick ping satisfied the Stop-hook orchestration-required gate before any work ran. Removed the entry-write; the marker is now written ONLY by real completion signals via a new recordOrchestrationCompletion helper: a chainLive settlement (task-settlement.ts) or a captain debrief with real agent verdicts (captain.ts, captured before the synthetic fallback). Reworded the tool description (quick no longer ''satisfies enforcement''). Enforcement now verifies completion (verdicts>0), not invocation — the framework''s central claim is finally true in code. Build clean; mcp 397→403, cli 409.'
